        <definition>DIE llvm::DIEUnit::Die</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>Die</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::DIEUnit::Die</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>The compile unit or type unit <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e" kindref="compound">DIE</ref>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This variable must be an instance of <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e" kindref="compound">DIE</ref> so that we can calculate the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e_unit" kindref="compound">DIEUnit</ref> from any <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e" kindref="compound">DIE</ref> by traversing the parent backchain and getting the Unit <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e" kindref="compound">DIE</ref>, and then casting itself to a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e_unit" kindref="compound">DIEUnit</ref>. This allows us to be able to find the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e_unit" kindref="compound">DIEUnit</ref> for any <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e" kindref="compound">DIE</ref> without having to store a pointer to the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e_unit" kindref="compound">DIEUnit</ref> in each <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e" kindref="compound">DIE</ref> instance. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
